  <middle>
    <section anchor="introduction" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-1">
      <name slugifiedName="name-introduction">Introduction</name>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-1-1"><xref target="RFC5959" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC5959"/> describes conventions necessary to protect the
AsymmetricKeyPackage content type <xref target="RFC5958" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC5958"/> with Cryptographic
Message Syntax (CMS) protecting the following content types:
SignedData <xref target="RFC5652" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC5652"/>, EnvelopedData <xref target="RFC5652" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC5652"/>, EncryptedData
<xref target="RFC5652" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC5652"/>, AuthenticatedData <xref target="RFC5652" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC5652"/>, and AuthEnvelopedData
<xref target="RFC5083" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC5083"/>.  This document amends <xref target="RFC5959" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC5959"/> by extending the
algorithms used with SignedData and EnvelopedData to include Elliptic
Curve Digital Signature Algorithm (ECDSA) and Elliptic Curve Diffie-Hellman
(ECDH), respectively.  Familiarity with <xref target="RFC5959" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC5959"/> and
<xref target="RFC5753" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC5753"/> is assumed.</t>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-1-2">This document does not define any new algorithms; instead, it refers
to previously defined algorithms.</t>
      <section anchor="terminology" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-1.1">
        <name slugifiedName="name-terminology">Terminology</name>
        <t indent="0" pn="section-1.1-1">The key words &quot;<bcp14>MUST</bcp14>&quot;, &quot;<bcp14>MUST NOT</bcp14>&quot;, &quot;<bcp14>REQUIRED</bcp14>&quot;, &quot;<bcp14>SHALL</bcp14>&quot;, &quot;<bcp14>SHALL NOT</bcp14>&quot;,
&quot;<bcp14>SHOULD</bcp14>&quot;, &quot;<bcp14>SHOULD NOT</bcp14>&quot;, &quot;<bcp14>RECOMMENDED</bcp14>&quot;, &quot;<bcp14>NOT RECOMMENDED</bcp14>&quot;, &quot;<bcp14>MAY</bcp14>&quot;, and
&quot;<bcp14>OPTIONAL</bcp14>&quot; in this document are to be interpreted as described in
<xref target="RFC2119" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC2119"/>.</t>
      </section>
    </section>
    <section anchor="asymmetrickeypackage" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-2">
      <name slugifiedName="name-asymmetrickeypackage">AsymmetricKeyPackage</name>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-2-1">As noted in Asymmetric Key Packages <xref target="RFC5958" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC5958"/>, CMS can be used to
protect the AsymmetricKeyPackage.  The following provides guidance
for SignedData <xref target="RFC5652" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC5652"/> and EnvelopedData <xref target="RFC5652" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC5652"/> when used with
Elliptic Curve algorithms.</t>
      <section anchor="signeddata" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-2.1">
        <name slugifiedName="name-signeddata">SignedData</name>
        <t indent="0" pn="section-2.1-1">If an implementation supports SignedData, then it <bcp14>MAY</bcp14> support ECDSA
<xref target="RFC6090" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC6090"/><xref target="RFC5753" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC5753"/>.</t>
      </section>
      <section anchor="envelopeddata" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-2.2">
        <name slugifiedName="name-envelopeddata">EnvelopedData</name>
        <t indent="0" pn="section-2.2-1">When key agreement is used, standard (as opposed to cofactor) ECDH
<xref target="RFC6090" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC6090"/><xref target="RFC5753" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC5753"/> <bcp14>MAY</bcp14> be supported.</t>
      </section>
    </section>
    <section anchor="public-key-sizes" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-3">
      <name slugifiedName="name-public-key-sizes">Public Key Sizes</name>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-3-1">The easiest way to implement SignedData and EnvelopedData is with
public key certificates <xref target="RFC5280" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC5280"/><xref target="RFC5480" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC5480"/>.  If an implementation
supports ECDSA or ECDH, then it <bcp14>MUST</bcp14> support keys on the P-256 curve.</t>
    </section>
    <section anchor="security-considerations" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-4">
      <name slugifiedName="name-security-considerations">Security Considerations</name>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-4-1">The security considerations from <xref target="RFC5280" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC5280"/>, <xref target="RFC5480" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC5480"/>, <xref target="RFC5652" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC5652"/>,
<xref target="RFC5753" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC5753"/>, <xref target="RFC5959" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC5959"/>, and <xref target="RFC6090" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC6090"/> apply.</t>
    </section>
  </middle>
